{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>On that day.</b> The branch of YHWH — some say it concerns Hezekiah, but what seems correct to me is that they are the righteous of Jerusalem who will escape." "<b>For splendor.</b> Like \"it is the splendor of all lands\" (Ezekiel 20:6); like splendor. Some say it is from the Aramaic root, as in למאן די יצבי יתננה (Daniel 4:14). And R. Moses the Kohen interpreted צמח literally, that HaShem will give blessing in the plant and in the fruit."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:52:15.421531466Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}